Built-in function names, from LVKit
===================================

File:     crates/buzzard-rsrc/src/blocks/heap/primitives.rs
Source:   LVKit, https://github.com/pragmatest-dev/lvkit
          src/lvkit/data/primitives/*.json
          commit b0430f03e4a6a0ce9b1015215efb1cce6d7509ff
Licence:  Apache License, Version 2.0 (full text in LICENSE)
          Copyright 2025-2026 Ryan Friedman

What was taken: for each built-in function, its resource id, its name, and
LVKit's `verified` flag. Nothing else was copied: no descriptions, no
documentation links, no terminal names, no code, and nothing from LVKit's
standard-library data (src/lvkit/data/vilib).

Changes made (Apache-2.0, section 4(b)): the data was modified. The entries
of 77 JSON files were flattened into one Rust table sorted by id, reduced to
the three fields above, and 3 entries whose name is a placeholder ("Unknown",
"Unknown ...") were left out, leaving 687 of 690. The table is produced by
tools/gen_primitives.py and is not edited by hand.

Provenance of the names: 487 of the 690 entries in LVKit (484 of the 687 kept
here) are tagged by LVKit as coming from "vi-scripting-nodes-lv2025". That is
a list of function ids, names and terminals that a third party produced with
the VI Scripting interface of LabVIEW 2025 and attached, without a licence
statement, to LVKit issue #59 (https://github.com/pragmatest-dev/lvkit/issues/59).
LVKit merged it into its table. buzzard takes the result from LVKit under
LVKit's licence and has not seen the original export. The owner of buzzard
accepted this origin knowingly: the names are facts about the file format,
not creative text. The table is kept in one generated file so that it can be
replaced by an independently derived one. buzzard has not checked any name
against LabVIEW; 162 entries are marked verified by LVKit, the rest are not.

